{
  "description": "Grants of a child run are a subset of its parent's pinned grant (P6.3). One table for Node (domain/child-runs.ts) and Python (harness_core.journal.children). `parent` patches the base parent spec's grants (sandboxProfile, egress). `depth` is the child's (a root run is 0). A refusal names its code, the dimension and the requested items it refuses; dimensions are checked in registry order and the first refusal is reported. A1: the access dimension's items are the parent's pinned route ids (Node modelRouteId, Python PinnedRoute.route_id); a route that pins a model account carries it in its id, so a child can only take the parent's own accounts; the child's model policy is the parent's routes it was granted, in the parent's order.",
